# CelebBoard — HubSpot Integration Implementation Guide

> Step-by-step plan: from creating a HubSpot developer account to a fully working OAuth + webhook + KPI integration with a visual trigger builder in the admin UI.

---

## Part 1: HubSpot Developer Account & App Setup

### Step 1 — Create a HubSpot Developer Account

1. Go to https://developers.hubspot.com/
2. Click "Create a developer account" (top right)
3. Sign up with a new email (or your existing HubSpot login — it will create a separate developer workspace)
4. You'll land in the developer portal — this is where you manage apps, not CRM data

> **Important distinction**: A developer account is NOT a HubSpot CRM portal. It's a workspace for building apps. You'll also need a test CRM portal to actually test with deals, contacts, etc.

### Step 2 — Create a Test Portal (Sandbox)

1. In the developer portal, go to **Testing** → **Test accounts** (left sidebar)
2. Click "Create app test account"
3. This gives you a full HubSpot CRM portal with fake data — deals, contacts, companies, etc.
4. Note the **Portal ID** (also called "Hub ID") — you'll see it in the top-right corner (e.g., `47329841`)
5. Add some test data: create a few deals in different stages, contacts, companies with properties filled in

### Step 3 — Create a HubSpot App

1. In the developer portal, go to **Apps** (left sidebar)
2. Click "Create app"
3. Fill in:
   - **App name**: `CelebBoard`
   - **Description**: `Team celebration platform — turns CRM wins into office TV celebrations`
   - **Logo**: Upload the CelebBoard logo
   - **Support URL**: `https://celebboard.com` (or your staging URL)
   - **Privacy policy URL**: `https://celebboard.com/legal/privacy`

### Step 4 — Configure OAuth Scopes

In your app settings, go to the **Auth** tab:

1. **Redirect URL**: Add these (all environments you'll test on):
   ```
   http://localhost:3000/api/integrations/hubspot/callback
   https://celebboard.vercel.app/api/integrations/hubspot/callback
   https://app.celebboard.com/api/integrations/hubspot/callback
   ```

2. **Required Scopes** — these are the permissions CelebBoard needs:
   ```
   crm.objects.contacts.read
   crm.objects.companies.read
   crm.objects.deals.read
   crm.objects.quotes.read
   crm.objects.owners.read
   crm.schemas.contacts.read
   crm.schemas.companies.read
   crm.schemas.deals.read
   crm.schemas.quotes.read
   crm.schemas.custom.read
   ```

   **Why each scope**:
   - `crm.objects.*.read` — Read object records (deals, contacts, etc.) for enrichment when webhooks fire, and for KPI queries
   - `crm.objects.owners.read` — Sync team members (owners) with photos
   - `crm.schemas.*.read` — Fetch all properties/fields on each object type (powers the dynamic dropdown UI in trigger builder)

3. Copy down your **Client ID** and **Client Secret** — you'll need these in your `.env`

### Step 5 — Configure Webhook Subscriptions

In your app settings, go to the **Webhooks** tab:

1. **Target URL**: `https://celebboard.vercel.app/api/webhooks/hubspot`
   - This is a SINGLE endpoint for ALL customers (HubSpot routes by portalId)
   - For local dev, you'll need a tunnel (ngrok or similar)

2. **Create subscriptions** for these events:

   | Object | Event Type | Why |
   |--------|-----------|-----|
   | Deals | `deal.propertyChange` | Detects stage changes, amount changes, any deal property update |
   | Deals | `deal.creation` | New deal created |
   | Contacts | `contact.propertyChange` | Contact property updates |
   | Contacts | `contact.creation` | New contact created |
   | Companies | `company.propertyChange` | Company property updates |
   | Companies | `company.creation` | New company created |
   | Quotes | `deal.propertyChange` | Quote property updates (HubSpot treats quotes as deals internally for some webhook events) |
   | Quotes | `deal.creation` | Quote created |

   > **Note**: Custom object webhooks require the custom object's `objectTypeId`. You'll subscribe to these dynamically when a customer connects and has custom objects.

3. Activate the subscriptions (they start paused)

### Step 6 — Environment Variables

Add these to your `.env.local` (and Vercel environment variables):

```bash
# HubSpot App (from developer portal → your app → Auth tab)
HUBSPOT_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
HUBSPOT_CLIENT_SECRET=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
HUBSPOT_APP_ID=123456

# Webhook verification
HUBSPOT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your-app-client-secret  
# (HubSpot uses your Client Secret to sign webhook payloads)

# OAuth redirect (match what you set in Step 4)
HUBSPOT_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/integrations/hubspot/callback
```

