## Part 2: Database Schema Changes

### New: `integration_schemas` Table

Caches each customer's HubSpot schema (object types + properties) so the trigger builder UI can show dynamic dropdowns without hitting HubSpot's API on every page load.

```sql
CREATE TABLE integration_schemas (
  id              uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  org_id          uuid REFERENCES organizations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  integration_id  uuid REFERENCES integrations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  
  -- Schema data
  object_type     text NOT NULL,             -- 'deals', 'contacts', 'companies', 'quotes', '2-123456' (custom)
  object_label    text NOT NULL,             -- 'Deals', 'Contacts', 'My Custom Object'
  properties      jsonb NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]', 
  -- Array of: { name, label, type, fieldType, options[], groupName, description }
  -- type: 'string', 'number', 'date', 'datetime', 'enumeration', 'bool'
  -- fieldType: 'text', 'textarea', 'select', 'checkbox', 'number', 'date', 'booleancheckbox'
  -- options: [{ label, value }] for enumeration types (e.g., deal stages, dropdown properties)
  
  pipeline_stages jsonb DEFAULT '[]',        -- For deals/tickets: [{ pipelineId, pipelineName, stages: [{ id, label }] }]
  
  cached_at       timestamptz DEFAULT now(),
  
  UNIQUE(integration_id, object_type)
);

-- RLS
ALTER TABLE integration_schemas ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "org_isolation" ON integration_schemas
  USING (org_id = get_user_org_id());
```

