## Part 3: OAuth Flow Implementation

### File: `src/app/api/integrations/hubspot/authorize/route.ts`

**What it does**: When a user clicks "Connect HubSpot" in the admin UI, redirect them to HubSpot's OAuth consent screen.

```
Admin UI → GET /api/integrations/hubspot/authorize?org_id=xxx
  → Generate state token (CSRF protection, encodes org_id)
  → Store state in a short-lived cookie or DB record
  → Redirect to: https://app.hubspot.com/oauth/authorize
      ?client_id=HUBSPOT_CLIENT_ID
      &redirect_uri=HUBSPOT_REDIRECT_URI
      &scope=crm.objects.deals.read crm.schemas.deals.read ...
      &state={encrypted_state_token}
```

### File: `src/app/api/integrations/hubspot/callback/route.ts`

**What it does**: HubSpot redirects back here after the user authorizes. Exchange the code for tokens.

```
HubSpot redirects → GET /api/integrations/hubspot/callback?code=xxx&state=xxx
  → Validate state token (CSRF check, extract org_id)
  → POST https://api.hubapi.com/oauth/v1/token
      grant_type=authorization_code
      code={code}
      redirect_uri={HUBSPOT_REDIRECT_URI}
      client_id={HUBSPOT_CLIENT_ID}
      client_secret={HUBSPOT_CLIENT_SECRET}
  → Receive: { access_token, refresh_token, expires_in }
  → GET https://api.hubapi.com/oauth/v1/access-tokens/{access_token}
      → Returns: { hub_id, hub_domain, user, scopes }
  → UPSERT into integrations table:
      org_id, type='hubspot', name='HubSpot',
      credentials: { access_token, refresh_token, token_expires_at, portal_id, hub_domain },
      config: { portal_id },
      status: 'active'
  → Trigger initial sync (schema + owners) — fire-and-forget or queue
  → Redirect to /app/integrations?connected=hubspot
```

### File: `src/lib/connectors/hubspot/auth.ts`

**Token refresh helper** — called before any HubSpot API request:

```
getValidToken(integration):
  → If token_expires_at > now() + 5 minutes: return access_token
  → Else: POST https://api.hubapi.com/oauth/v1/token
      grant_type=refresh_token
      refresh_token={integration.credentials.refresh_token}
      client_id, client_secret
  → Update integration.credentials with new tokens
  → Return fresh access_token
```

