## Part 6: Object Enrichment Service

### File: `src/lib/connectors/hubspot/enrichment.ts`

```
enrichObject(integration, objectType, objectId, requestedProperties):

  token = await getValidToken(integration)
  
  // Build properties list from all triggers that might fire
  // Plus standard useful fields (name, amount, owner, etc.)
  properties = [...requestedProperties, ...getDefaultProperties(objectType)]
  
  GET https://api.hubapi.com/crm/v3/objects/{objectType}/{objectId}
    ?properties={properties.join(',')}
    &associations=companies,contacts,deals
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer {token}
  
  Returns: {
    id: '7890',
    properties: {
      dealname: 'Acme Corp Annual License',
      dealstage: 'closedwon',
      amount: '24500',
      closedate: '2026-03-05',
      hubspot_owner_id: '12345',
      pipeline: 'default',
      hs_deal_stage_probability: '1.0',
      custom_field_x: 'some value',
      ...
    },
    associations: {
      companies: { results: [{ id: '456', type: 'deal_to_company' }] },
      contacts: { results: [{ id: '789', type: 'deal_to_contact' }] }
    }
  }
  
  // If there are associations and the field_mapping references them,
  // fetch associated objects too:
  // e.g., company name from the associated company
  if (needsAssociatedData) {
    companyData = GET /crm/v3/objects/companies/{associatedCompanyId}?properties=name,domain
    contactData = GET /crm/v3/objects/contacts/{associatedContactId}?properties=firstname,lastname,email
  }
  
  return mergedEnrichedObject  // flat object with all properties + association data
```

### Association Field Mapping Convention

For the field mapping system, use dot-notation to reference associated objects:

```json
{
  "deal_name": "dealname",
  "amount": "amount",
  "company_name": "associations.companies.name",
  "contact_email": "associations.contacts.email",
  "owner_id": "hubspot_owner_id"
}
```

The enrichment service resolves `associations.companies.name` by:
1. Getting the associated company ID from the deal's associations
2. Fetching the company record
3. Extracting the `name` property

