## Part 14: Local Development with HubSpot Webhooks

HubSpot needs to reach your webhook endpoint. During local development:

### Option A: ngrok (recommended)

```bash
# Install ngrok
brew install ngrok  # or download from ngrok.com

# Start your Next.js dev server
pnpm dev  # runs on localhost:3000

# In another terminal, start ngrok
ngrok http 3000

# You'll get a URL like: https://abc123.ngrok-free.app
# Set this as your webhook target URL in HubSpot developer portal:
# https://abc123.ngrok-free.app/api/webhooks/hubspot

# Also update HUBSPOT_REDIRECT_URI in .env.local:
# HUBSPOT_REDIRECT_URI=https://abc123.ngrok-free.app/api/integrations/hubspot/callback
```

### Option B: HubSpot CLI (webhook replay)

```bash
# HubSpot also offers a CLI that can replay webhook events
# Useful for testing without waiting for real events
npx @hubspot/cli webhook replay --app-id=123456
```

### Testing Without Webhooks

For early development, you can skip webhooks entirely and test with:
1. The simulation endpoint you already have (`/api/simulate`)
2. Manually creating celebrations via the admin UI
3. The "Test Trigger" feature that evaluates conditions against existing HubSpot objects

